    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0342" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/68: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-05-30T18:00:00+01:00">May 30, 1934—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 30—3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>287. Department’s 211, May 24, 3 p.m.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d190-f1"/> The
                    Japanese Ambassador informed me today he was accepting the British invitation
                    [along?] very much the same lines as our reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d190-f1" n="54" xml:id="d190-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 202, May 24, 3 p.m., to the Ambassador in France, <ref
                        target="#pg239">p. 239</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
